  "_school_comment": "Division renames. The source rewrote its division vocabulary between the Apr 2025 and Sep 2025 records requests: 20 names retired, 34 appeared, and 61% of the Apr 2025 rows ended up under a name that no longer exists — which severs every division time series at that boundary. Keys are the retired name, values the name in use now. A pair belongs here only when the two names are the same unit: at least 85% of the people under the old name reappear under the new one in the next snapshot, or the names match once case and punctuation are stripped. Three divisions that lost their names fail that test and are deliberately absent because they reorganized rather than renamed — General Services (27% to Office of Human Resources), Division of Student Life (66%), General Educational Admin (51%); aliasing those would invent history. `npm run data` reports any division that disappears between snapshots, with where its people went, so the next rename shows up as build output. The Administrative Transformation Program became the Workday Enterprise Solutions Team in two steps: 91 of its 117 continuing people were under the new name by Mar 2026 (87% of WEST's first members), and the last of them, with the three from Administration Innovation and Planning, by Sep 2026.",
