  "_department_comment": "Department renames, keyed \"School|Old department\" with the school's name after the `school` block above (the source reuses department names across schools). A pair belongs here only when the two names are one unit, judged both ways by where the people went: at least 75% of the old department's continuing people sit in the new one, at least three of them, and at least 75% of the new department's continuing people came from the old — and from no other department also sending most of its people there. Several departments sending to one new department are a merger, and are left out on purpose: carrying one files every older, finer unit under the new name and wipes its history (Mar 2026, when Vet Med and Pharmacy put every department under \"Divisionwide\", reads as twenty units merging). Renames chain (A to B, later B to C: A reads C). A name that comes back into use is not a key: Campus Planning and Design became Planning and Design, then Planning & Design, then Campus Planning and Design again. `npm run data` checks every step with this rule (scripts/lib/normalize.mjs `departmentChanges`), reports any rename not carried here, and publishes each step's renames, mergers and other departments that ended on the Data page.",
